# ── Site URL ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Used for canonical tags, the sitemap, robots.txt and the Open Graph image
# URL. You do NOT need to set this on Vercel: the build falls back to Vercel's
# own production domain automatically. Set it only once you point a custom
# domain at the site, because that is the one thing the fallback cannot know.
# No trailing slash.

NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=

# ── Google Search Console ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Optional. Google will index the site without it; what verification buys you
# is the ability to submit the sitemap and to see which searches you actually
# appear in — the only real feedback loop SEO has.
#
#   1. search.google.com/search-console → Add property → URL prefix.
#   2. Choose the "HTML tag" method and copy ONLY the content="…" value,
#      not the whole tag.
#   3. Set it here (or on Vercel), redeploy, then press Verify.
#   4. Afterwards: Sitemaps → submit "sitemap.xml".

GOOGLE_SITE_VERIFICATION=

# ── Google AdSense ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The publisher id is COMMITTED in src/lib/ads.ts, so ads work out of the box
# with nothing set here. A ca-pub- id is public by design — it is printed in
# the page source and in /ads.txt of every AdSense site — so this is not a
# secret being checked in.
#
# Override these only for a fork or a second property:
#
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_ADSENSE_CLIENT   ca-pub-0000000000000000
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_ADSENSE_SLOT     0000000000   (one display unit's slot id)
#
# The slot id is the piece that is still missing. AdSense will not let you
# create an ad unit until the site is approved, so "client set, slot empty" is
# the normal state for days, and the <ins> stays unrendered until both exist.
# Once approved: Ads → By ad unit → Display ads → Create; the snippet it hands
# you contains data-ad-slot="0000000000".
#
# Note: NEXT_PUBLIC_ vars are inlined at build time, so changing them on
# Vercel requires a redeploy, not just a restart.

NEXT_PUBLIC_ADSENSE_CLIENT=
NEXT_PUBLIC_ADSENSE_SLOT=

# ── Google Analytics 4 ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The measurement id is COMMITTED in src/lib/analytics.ts, so analytics work
# with nothing set here. Override only for a fork or a second property.
#
#   Admin → Data streams → Web → "Measurement ID", shaped G-XXXXXXXXXX. It is
#   NOT the numeric "Stream ID" next to it, and not a UA- id (GA3, dead).
#
# The tag is always on the page under Consent Mode v2 with cookies DENIED by
# default; accepting the banner flips it to granted. Google's "tag detected"
# check passes because the tag is in the HTML; cookies still wait for a yes.

NEXT_PUBLIC_GA_ID=
